Description: fftools: paced self-decode for -map_inlineass (drop the null-mux decode-sink)
 vf_inlineass only receives cues while the bound subtitle stream is actively
 decoded (scaleplex_inlineass_handle_subtitle fires from transcode_subtitles,
 patch 0100). Until now the worker rewriter forced that by appending a throwaway
 output `-map <spec> -f null -codec ass|dvdsub nullfile`, which spins up a full
 demux->subdec->subenc->null-mux chain on its own scheduler threads.
 .
 That output is an independent, throttle-exempt consumer of the input. The
 canThrottle sleep (patch 0097) lands only in the video encoder thread, so once
 PMS asserts throttle the single demux thread blocks on the video queue and the
 sub path paces with it — fine. But during the pre-throttle flat-out buffer
 fill, the redundant sub decode + ass/dvdsub re-encode + null-mux threads
 compete with the video path for the NFS read and CPU at exactly the moment the
 client buffer is being filled. On long embedded-sub 4K titles this surfaces as
 regular playback skips during fill that vanish once throttle equilibrates
 (embedded subs only — sidecar subs are a small separate file). The sub
 re-encode to /dev/null is pure waste; we only ever wanted the decoder to RUN.
 .
 Fix: decode the -map_inlineass stream with a sink-less decoder created directly
 from the binding. No output stream, no encoder, no muxer. Pacing is correct by
 construction: the decoder has no downstream, so sch_dec_send discards each
 frame immediately and its input queue never blocks the demux; the demux is a
 single sequential thread, so it advances in file order at video pace (the only
 stream that blocks it is video, gated by the canThrottle sleep). No independent
 consumer => no extra read-ahead during fill. This mirrors Plex 6.x's
 single-threaded loop (sub decoded inline with video) inside jellyfin 7.x's
 split-thread scheduler.
 .
 Scheduler support for a sink-less decoder (sch_add_dec auto-creates output 0,
 and two sites assume an output has a sink):
 .
   - SchDec gains `sink_less`; sch_dec_set_sinkless() sets it.
   - start_prepare() skips the "Decoder output not connected to any sink" check
     for a sink-less decoder (the source check still applies).
   - sch_dec_send() discards the frame and returns 0 when the target output has
     nb_dst == 0 (otherwise it returns AVERROR_EOF -> process_subtitle returns
     AVERROR_EXIT -> the decoder thread would stop after the first subtitle).
 .
 ist_inlineass_add() in ffmpeg_demux.c drives ist_use() (idempotent: allocs the
 decoder + connects demux->dec exactly like the normal decode path), drops the
 returned decoder-output node (connects it to nothing), and marks the decoder
 sink-less. scaleplex_inlineass_setup_decoders() calls it for every binding;
 ffmpeg.c invokes that just before sch_start().
 .
 Worker rewriter change (separate commit): stop emitting the
 `-map <spec> -f null -codec ass|dvdsub nullfile` sink in every path; keep
 `-map_inlineass <spec>`, which now drives the decode on its own.
Origin: scaleplex; design ref docs/PACED_SELF_DECODE.md, Plex Transcoder plex.c
Forwarded: not-needed
Author: scaleplex
Last-Update: 2026-05-25
---
diff --git a/fftools/ffmpeg.c b/fftools/ffmpeg.c
index c5f7419..7476b47 100644
--- a/fftools/ffmpeg.c
+++ b/fftools/ffmpeg.c
@@ -80,6 +80,7 @@
 #include "cmdutils.h"
 #include "ffmpeg.h"
 #include "ffmpeg_sched.h"
+#include "scaleplex_inlineass.h"
 #include "ffmpeg_utils.h"
 
 const char program_name[] = "ffmpeg";
@@ -944,6 +945,14 @@ static int transcode(Scheduler *sch)
 
     atomic_store(&transcode_init_done, 1);
 
+    /* scaleplex: create sink-less decoders for every -map_inlineass binding
+     * so embedded subtitle streams decode (feeding vf_inlineass via the
+     * side-channel) without a throwaway null-mux output. Must run before
+     * sch_start() validates the graph. No-op when -map_inlineass unused. */
+    ret = scaleplex_inlineass_setup_decoders();
+    if (ret < 0)
+        return ret;
+
     ret = sch_start(sch);
     if (ret < 0)
         return ret;
diff --git a/fftools/ffmpeg.h b/fftools/ffmpeg.h
index 507b4db..dea63b7 100644
--- a/fftools/ffmpeg.h
+++ b/fftools/ffmpeg.h
@@ -899,6 +899,12 @@ int ifile_open(const OptionsContext *o, const char *filename, Scheduler *sch);
 void ifile_close(InputFile **f);
 
 int ist_output_add(InputStream *ist, OutputStream *ost);
+
+/* scaleplex: ensure an embedded subtitle stream is decoded for the
+ * vf_inlineass side-channel feed, with no output stream. Creates a
+ * sink-less decoder + connects the demuxer stream to it. Idempotent on
+ * the underlying stream's decoder. Returns the decoder's sch index. */
+int ist_inlineass_add(InputStream *ist);
 int ist_filter_add(InputStream *ist, InputFilter *ifilter, int is_simple,
                    const ViewSpecifier *vs, InputFilterOptions *opts,
                    SchedulerNode *src);
diff --git a/fftools/ffmpeg_demux.c b/fftools/ffmpeg_demux.c
index 8135432..a5d8201 100644
--- a/fftools/ffmpeg_demux.c
+++ b/fftools/ffmpeg_demux.c
@@ -1009,6 +1009,34 @@ int ist_output_add(InputStream *ist, OutputStream *ost)
     return ost->enc ? ds->sch_idx_dec : ds->sch_idx_stream;
 }
 
+int ist_inlineass_add(InputStream *ist)
+{
+    Demuxer      *d  = demuxer_from_ifile(ist->file);
+    DemuxStream  *ds = ds_from_ist(ist);
+    SchedulerNode src;
+    int ret;
+
+    /* scaleplex: create a decoder for an embedded subtitle stream that is
+     * consumed only through the vf_inlineass side-channel (no output
+     * stream). ist_use() is idempotent: it allocs the decoder + connects
+     * the demux stream to its input exactly like a normal decode path. We
+     * intentionally DROP `src` (the decoder output node) — connect it to
+     * nothing — then mark the decoder sink-less so the scheduler tolerates
+     * the unconnected output and discards decoded frames. The decode
+     * itself fires scaleplex_inlineass_handle_subtitle() in ffmpeg_dec.c,
+     * feeding the bound filter. Paced by the demux interleave (single demux
+     * thread, video-read backpressure) — no separate null-mux consumer to
+     * race the file read ahead during buffer fill. */
+    ret = ist_use(ist, DECODING_FOR_FILTER, NULL, &src);
+    if (ret < 0)
+        return ret;
+    (void)src;
+
+    sch_dec_set_sinkless(d->sch, ds->sch_idx_dec);
+
+    return ds->sch_idx_dec;
+}
+
 int ist_filter_add(InputStream *ist, InputFilter *ifilter, int is_simple,
                    const ViewSpecifier *vs, InputFilterOptions *opts,
                    SchedulerNode *src)
